= Rákosi Takes the Floor

Mátyás Rákosi is small, bald and very sure of himself. Serrati, he says, chose Turati over the International, and anyone who defends Serrati has made the same choice. The German party, he adds, looking at nobody in particular, may need a Livorno of its own.

The members who have not made up their minds look at the Zentrale's end of the table.

- @answer: Answer him point by point.
- @mandate: Ask by what mandate he speaks to a German committee.
- @silence: Let him finish, and say nothing.

@answer
subtitle: Our best speaker against Moscow's envoy. It depends on who that is.
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.sway((0.06 + Math.random() * 0.05) * Q.congress_speaker_power);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -2);
!}

[+ congress_speaker_name +] answers for forty minutes: on Italy, on Serrati's workers, on what a split costs when it is made by telegram. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] members are seen nodding, and they vote that way too. ?][? if congress_last_moved = 0 : It is a fine speech, and nobody moves. ?]

@mandate
subtitle: Some members will admire the question. Moscow will not.
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.sway(0.05 + Math.random() * 0.04);
RG.congress.bitter(3);
Q.independence += 4;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -6);
!}

Rákosi answers that he speaks for the World Congress, which is to say for all of us. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] members decide they do not like being spoken for. ?] Frölich calls the question a provocation.

@silence
subtitle: He gains ground. Nobody can say we insulted the International.
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.lose(0.04);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 3);
!}

The Zentrale thanks Rákosi and moves to the next speaker. A few waverers take the silence as an answer.
